diff --git a/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt b/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt
index 4a8d880..b87d049 100644
--- a/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt
+++ b/ComicRack/Output/Changes.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-﻿orbitdesign Build 1.69 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
+﻿orbitdesign Build 1.70 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
 
 * 1.1 FIX: Hardware acceleration stability. Fixed OpenGL extension detection, replaced the deprecated automatic mip map generation that crashed some drivers, checked texture uploads for errors, and added a startup guard that switches hardware acceleration off for one session if ComicRack failed to start last time.
 * 1.2 NEW: Direct2D renderer for the reader. Used by default when hardware acceleration is on, with OpenGL and then software rendering as fallbacks. Handles graphics device resets, uses high quality cubic sampling for "Enable Hardware Filters", and supports paper textures. Start with -hwgl to use the old OpenGL renderer.
@@ -69,6 +69,7 @@
 * 1.67 NEW: Middle mouse click in the reader turns the magnifier on and off (Toggle Magnifier, alongside M). It is added once to your saved keyboard layout and can be changed or removed in Preferences > Keyboard. Also gave the middle-button zoom drag the same few pixels of give as the left-button drag, so a click with a slightly unsteady hand is no longer mistaken for a drag.
 * 1.68 CHANGE: The magnifier is now a round lens instead of a rectangle, and 15% bigger (the longer side of your chosen size plus 15%, so it covers more of the page). The Glass style has a metal rim and a soft reflection, the Simple style a thin dark rim; clicks in the empty corners around the lens go to the page underneath. Round needs hardware acceleration (Direct2D); with other renderers it stays rectangular, also 15% bigger. Also fixed the magnified picture sitting a few pixels off and rotating about the wrong point on rotated pages.
 * 1.69 CHANGE: The Glass magnifier now uses the engraved magnifying glass artwork: the zoomed view sits inside its ring, with the handle hanging off to the lower right. The lens is still the 15% larger round view (the artwork scales to fit it). The Simple style keeps its plain round rim, and renderers without hardware acceleration keep the rectangular frame.
+* 1.70 CHANGE: Updated the magnifier artwork and gave it a soft drop shadow, cast down and to the right, outside the lens.
 
 
 Community Edition Build 0.9.184:
diff --git a/ComicRack/Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs b/ComicRack/Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs
